{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-mat-12-1","title":"Matthew 12:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Christ reproves the blindness of the Pharisees concerning the breach of the sabbath, 3 by scripture, 9 by reason, 13 and by a miracle. 22 He heals a man possessed that was blind and dumb; 24 and confuting the absurd charge of casting out devils by Beelzebub, he shows that blasphemy against the Holy Ghost shall never be forgiven. 36 Account shall be made of idle words. 38 He rebukes the unfaithful, who seek after a sign, 46 and shows who is his brother, sister, and mother.</p>\n<p>went. Mr 2:23-28; Lu 6:1-5 to pluck. De 23:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-2","title":"Matthew 12:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Behold. 10; Ex 20:9-11; 23:12; 31:15-17; 35:2; Nu 15:32-36; Isa 58:13 Mr 3:2-5; Lu 6:6-11; 13:10-17; 23:56; Joh 5:9-11,16,17; 7:21-24 Joh 9:14-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-3","title":"Matthew 12:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Have. 5; 19:4; 21:16; 22:31; Mr 12:10,26; Lu 6:3; 10:26 what. 1Sa 21:3-6; Mr 2:25,26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-4","title":"Matthew 12:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>the shew-bread. Ex 25:30; Le 24:5-9 but. Ex 29:32,33; Le 8:31; 24:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-5","title":"Matthew 12:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>on. Nu 28:9,10; Joh 7:22,23 profane. Ne 13:17; Eze 24:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-6","title":"Matthew 12:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>41,42; 23:17-21; 2Ch 6:18; Hag 2:7-9; Mal 3:1; Joh 2:19-21 Eph 2:20-22; Col 2:9; 1Pe 2:4,5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-7","title":"Matthew 12:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>if. 9:13; 22:29; Ac 13:27 I will.That is, I desire, or require mercy, or acts of humanity, rather than sacrifice.</p>\n<p>Isa 1:11-17; Ho 6:6; Mic 6:6-8 condemned. Job 32:3; Ps 94:21; 109:31; Pr 17:15; Jas 5:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-8","title":"Matthew 12:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>9:6; Mr 2:28; 9:4-7; Lu 6:5; Joh 5:17-23; 1Co 9:21; 16:2 Re 1:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-9","title":"Matthew 12:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>he went. Mr 3:1-5; Lu 6:6-11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-10","title":"Matthew 12:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>which. 1Ki 13:4-6; Zec 11:17; Joh 5:3 Is it. 19:3; 22:17,18; Lu 13:14; 14:3-6; 20:22; Joh 5:10; 9:16 that. Isa 32:6; 59:4,13; Lu 6:6,7; 11:54; 23:2,14; Joh 8:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-11","title":"Matthew 12:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>what.This was an {argumentum ad hominem.} The Jews held that such things were lawful on the sabbath day, and our Saviour very properly appealed to their canons in vindication of his intention to heal the distressed man.</p>\n<p>Lu 13:15-17; 14:5 and if. Ex 23:4,5; De 22:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-12","title":"Matthew 12:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>is a. 6:26; Lu 12:24 it is. Mr 3:4; Lu 6:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-13","title":"Matthew 12:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>and it. Lu 13:13; Ac 3:7,8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-14","title":"Matthew 12:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>went. 27:1; Mr 3:6; Lu 6:11; Joh 5:18; 10:39; 11:53,57 held a council. or, took counsel.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-15","title":"Matthew 12:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>he withdrew. 10:23; Lu 6:12; Joh 7:1; 10:40-42; 11:54 great. 4:24,25; 19:2; Mr 3:7-12; 6:56; Lu 6:17-19; Joh 9:4; Ga 6:9 1Pe 2:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-16","title":"Matthew 12:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>9:30; 17:9; Mr 7:36; Lu 5:14,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-17","title":"Matthew 12:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>it. 8:17; 13:35; 21:4; Isa 41:22,23; 42:9; 44:26; Lu 21:22; 24:44 Joh 10:35; 12:38; 19:28; Ac 13:27 saying. Isa 42:1-4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-18","title":"Matthew 12:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>Behold.This prophecy is expressly referred to the Messiah by the Targumist, who renders, \"Behold my servant the Messiah,\" etc., {ha avdi mesheecha;} and it was amply fulfilled in the gentle, lowly, condescending and beneficent nature of Christ's miracles and personal ministry, his perseverance in the midst of opposition, without engaging in contentious disputation, and his kind and tender dealing with weak and tempted believers.</p>\n<p>my servant. Isa 49:5,6; 52:13; 53:11; Zec 3:8; Php 2:6,7 whom I. Ps 89:19; Isa 49:1-3; Lu 23:35; 1Pe 2:4 my beloved. 3:17; 17:5; Mr 1:11; 9:7; Lu 9:35; Eph 1:6; Col 1:1,13; *marg: 2Pe 1:17 I will. 3:16; Isa 11:2; 59:20,21; 61:1-3; Lu 3:22; 4:18; Joh 1:32-34; 3:34 Ac 10:38 and he. Isa 32:15,16; 49:6; 60:2,3; 62:2; Jer 16:19; Lu 2:31,32; Ac 11:18 Ac 13:46-48; 14:27; 26:17,18; Ro 15:9-12; Eph 2:11-13; 3:5-8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-19","title":"Matthew 12:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>11:29; Zec 9:9; Lu 17:20; Joh 18:36-38; 2Co 10:1; 2Ti 2:24,25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-20","title":"Matthew 12:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>bruised. 11:28; 2Ki 18:21; Ps 51:17; 147:3; Isa 40:11; 57:15; 61:1-3 La 3:31-34; Eze 34:16; Lu 4:18; 2Co 2:7; Heb 12:12,13 till. Ps 98:1-3; Isa 42:3,4; Ro 15:17-19; 2Co 2:14; 10:3-5; Re 6:2 Re 19:11-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-21","title":"Matthew 12:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>Isa 11:10; Ro 15:12,13; Eph 1:12,13; Col 1:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-22","title":"Matthew 12:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>was. 9:32; Mr 3:11; Lu 11:14 he healed. Mr 7:35-37; 9:17-26 blind. Ps 51:15; Isa 29:18; 32:3,4; 35:5,6; Ac 26:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-23","title":"Matthew 12:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>the people. 9:33; 15:30,31 Is not. 9:27; 15:22; 21:9; 22:42,43; Joh 4:29; 7:40-42</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-24","title":"Matthew 12:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>when. 9:34; Mr 3:22; Lu 11:15 Beelzebub. Gr. Beelzebul, and so. 27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-25","title":"Matthew 12:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>Jesus. 9:4; Ps 139:2; Jer 17:10; Am 4:13; Mr 2:8; Joh 2:24,25; 21:17 1Co 2:11; Heb 4:13; Re 2:23 Every kingdom. Isa 9:21; 19:2,3; Mr 3:23-26; Lu 11:17,18; Ga 5:15; Re 16:19 Re 17:16,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-26","title":"Matthew 12:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>his. Joh 12:31; 14:30; 16:11; 2Co 4:4; Col 1:13; 1Jo 5:19; Re 9:11 Re 12:9; 16:10; 20:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-27","title":"Matthew 12:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>Beelzebub. 24 by whom. Mr 9:38,39; Lu 9:49,50; 11:19; Ac 19:13-16 they. 12:41,42; Lu 19:22; Ro 3:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-28","title":"Matthew 12:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>I cast. 18; Mr 16:17; Lu 11:20; Ac 10:38 then. 6:33; 21:31,43; Isa 9:6,7; Da 2:44; 7:14; Mr 1:15; 11:10 Lu 1:32,33; 9:2; 10:11; 11:20; 16:16; 17:20,21; Ro 14:17; Col 1:13 Heb 12:28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-29","title":"Matthew 12:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>Isa 49:24; 53:12; Mr 3:27; Lu 11:21,22; 1Jo 3:8; 4:4; Re 12:7-10 Re 20:1-3,7-9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-30","title":"Matthew 12:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>that is. 6:24; Jos 5:13; 24:15; 1Ch 12:17,18; Mr 9:40; Lu 9:50; 11:23 2Co 6:15,16; 1Jo 2:19; Re 3:15,16 gathereth. Ge 49:10; Ho 1:11; Joh 11:52</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-31","title":"Matthew 12:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>All. Isa 1:18; 55:7; Eze 33:11; 1Ti 1:13-15; Heb 6:4; *etc: Heb 10:26,29; 1Jo 1:9; 2:1,2 blasphemy.Blasphemy, [blasphemia ,] either from [blapto ten phemen,] to hurt, or blast the reputation, or from [ballo tais phemais,] to smite with words, or reports, when applied to men denotes injurious speaking, or calumny, and when used in reference to God signifies speaking impiously of his nature, attributes, and works.</p>\n<p>but. Mr 3:28-30; Lu 12:10; Ac 7:51; 1Jo 5:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-32","title":"Matthew 12:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>whosoever. 11:19; 13:55; Lu 7:34; 23:34; Joh 7:12,52; Ac 3:14,15,19 Ac 26:9-11; 1Ti 1:13,15 but. Joh 7:39; Heb 6:4-6; 10:26-29 it shall not. Job 36:13; Mr 3:29; Lu 16:23-26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-33","title":"Matthew 12:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>make the good tree. 23:26; Eze 18:31; Am 5:15; Lu 11:39,40; Jas 4:8 and his fruit good. 3:8-10; 7:16-20; Lu 3:9; 6:43,44; Joh 15:4-7; Jas 3:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-34","title":"Matthew 12:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>generation. 3:7; 23:33; Lu 3:7; Joh 8:44; 1Jo 3:10 how. 1Sa 24:13; Ps 10:6,7; 52:2-5; 53:1; 64:3,5; 120:2-4; 140:2,3 Isa 32:6; 59:4,14; Jer 7:2-5; Ro 3:10-14; Jas 3:5-8 for. Lu 6:45</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-35","title":"Matthew 12:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>good man. 13:52; Ps 37:30,31; Pr 10:20,21; 12:6,17-19; 15:4,23,28 Pr 16:21-23; 25:11,12; Eph 4:29; Col 3:16; 4:6 and an. 34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-36","title":"Matthew 12:36","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>every. Ec 12:14; Ro 2:16; Eph 6:4-6; Jude 1:14,15; Re 20:12 idle word.[Rhema ,] [argos ,] i.e., [ergo--work/act/deed,] from a, privative, and [ergon ,] work, a word that produces no good effect, and is not calculated to produce any. \"Discourse,\" says Dr. Doddridge, \"tending to innocent mirth, to exhilarate the spirits, is not idle discourse; as the time spent in necessary recreation is not idle time.\"</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-37","title":"Matthew 12:37","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>For by. Pr 13:3 justified. Jas 2:21-25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-38","title":"Matthew 12:38","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":38,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":38},"content":"<p>Master. 16:1-4; Mr 8:11,12; Lu 11:16,29; Joh 2:18; 4:48; 1Co 1:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-39","title":"Matthew 12:39","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":39,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":39},"content":"<p>adulterous. Isa 57:3; Mr 8:38; Jas 4:4 no sign. 16:4; Lu 11:29,30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-40","title":"Matthew 12:40","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":40,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":40},"content":"<p>as. Jon 1:17 so. 16:21; 17:23; 27:40,63,64; Joh 2:19 in the heart. Ps 63:9; Jon 2:2-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-41","title":"Matthew 12:41","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>men. Lu 11:32 rise. 42; Isa 54:17; Jer 3:11; Eze 16:51,52; Ro 2:27; Heb 11:7 this. 39,45; 16:4; 17:17; 23:36 because. Jon 3:5-10 behold. 6,42; Joh 3:31; 4:12; 8:53-58; Heb 3:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-42","title":"Matthew 12:42","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":42,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":42},"content":"<p>queen. 1Ki 10:1-13; 2Ch 9:1-12; Lu 11:31,32; Ac 8:27,28 hear. 1Ki 3:9,12,28; 4:29,34; 5:12; 10:4,7,24 behold. 3:17; 17:5; Isa 7:14; 9:6,7; Joh 1:14,18; Php 2:6,7; Heb 1:2-4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-43","title":"Matthew 12:43","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":43,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":43},"content":"<p>when.Had there been no reality in demoniacal possessions, as some have supposed, our Lord would scarcely have appealed to a case of this kind here, to point out the real state of the Jewish people, and their approaching desolation. Had this been only a vulgar error, of the nonsense of which the learned scribes and wise Pharisees must have been convinced, the case, not being in point, because not true, must have been treated with contempt by the very people for whose conviction it was designed.</p>\n<p>the unclean. Lu 11:24; Ac 8:13 he. Job 1:7; 2:2; 1Pe 5:8 dry. Ps 63:1; Isa 35:6,7; 41:18; Eze 47:8-12; Am 8:11-13 seeking. 8:29; Mr 5:7-13; Lu 8:28-32</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-44","title":"Matthew 12:44","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":44,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":44},"content":"<p>my. 29; Lu 11:21,22; Joh 13:27; Eph 2:2; 1Jo 4:4 he findeth. 13:20-22; Ps 81:11,12; Ho 7:6; Joh 12:6; 13:2; Ac 5:1-3; 8:18-23 1Co 11:19; 2Th 2:9-12; 1Ti 6:4,5,9,10; 1Jo 2:19; Jude 1:4,5 Re 13:3,4,8,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-45","title":"Matthew 12:45","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":45,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":45},"content":"<p>seven. 24; Mr 5:9; 16:9; Eph 6:12 more. 23:15 and the. Lu 11:26; Heb 6:4-8; 10:26-31,39; 2Pe 2:14-22; 1Jo 5:16,17 Jude 1:10-13 Even.And so it was; for they became worse and worse, as if totally abandoned to diabolical influence, till the besom of destruction swept them away.</p>\n<p>21:38-44; 23:32-39,24,34; Lu 11:49-51; 19:41-44; Joh 15:22-24 Ro 11:8-10; 1Th 2:15,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-46","title":"Matthew 12:46","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":46,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":46},"content":"<p>yet. Mr 2:21; 3:31-35; Lu 8:10,19-21 his. 13:55; Mr 6:3; Joh 2:12; 7:3,5,10; Ac 1:14; 1Co 9:5; Ga 1:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-48","title":"Matthew 12:48","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":48,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":48},"content":"<p>Who is. 10:37; De 33:9; Mr 3:32,33; Lu 2:49,52; Joh 2:3,4; 2Co 5:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-49","title":"Matthew 12:49","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":49,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":49},"content":"<p>his disciples. 28:7; Mr 3:34; Joh 17:8,9,20; 20:17-20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-12-50","title":"Matthew 12:50","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":50,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":50},"content":"<p>do. 7:20,21; 17:5; Mr 3:35; Lu 8:21; 11:27,28; Joh 6:29,40; 15:14 Ac 3:22,23; 16:30,31; 17:30; 26:20; Ga 5:6; 6:15; Col 3:11; Heb 5:9 Jas 1:21,22; 1Pe 4:2; 1Jo 2:17; 3:23,24; Re 22:14 the same. 25:40,45; 28:10; Ps 22:22; Joh 20:17; Ro 8:29; Heb 2:11-17 and sister. So 4:9,10,12; 5:1,2; 1Co 9:5; 2Co 11:2; Eph 5:25-27 and mother. Joh 19:26,27; 1Ti 5:2</p>"}]}